Section G: Local Traffic Authority 
18.* (a) Unless otherwise instructed by the central traffic authority, a local traffic authority may, after consulting with a police officer or a military police officer (regarding roads in military areas within the command area), place, mark, or remove in any way within its jurisdiction – 
(1) Warning signs, except for sign A-43 which means instruction; 
(1a) Instruction signs B-30, B-31, which will be valid only during nighttime; 
(2) Information signs, except for signs G-2 and G-7; 
