Guidelines for Street Planning in Cities - Pedestrian Traffic / Functions of the Sidewalk

The sidewalk is the part of the street designated for the movement and activities of pedestrians. In addition, the sidewalk also serves as a venue for additional components, both mobile and stationary, some of which are mentioned below:

A. Pedestrian Activities
- Pedestrian movement along the street;
- Pedestrian activities resulting from the function of the street side, such as commerce, public services, etc.;
- Special pedestrian activities on the street, such as gatherings, meetings, waiting;
- Markets, displays, etc.;
- Connection activities to transportation means, such as waiting for public transport, entering and exiting parked vehicles, entering and exiting underground public transport levels.

B. Motor Vehicle Activities
- Crossing the sidewalk at the entrance to the side (beyond parking in lots);
- Service area for service vehicles (loading and unloading area, fire lanes). 

